       "reasons": [
        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/pf050rx0162.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "stamped, not written: five serif figures in black ink across the roll, both panels agree. 2, 1, 4 and 2 are plain. The last has a closed upper loop over a closed bowl, so 8 rather than 6; if it were 6 the year would be 1926. Read as day.month.year with the separators dropped, 21.4.28, which falls after the 1904-1926 span of the readings so far. A faint half-inked mark stands a digit's width before the 2 and a dot follows the last figure. Crops 1 and 2 hold only perforations and brown stains."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
